<section class="chapter" aria-label="Shared architecture">
  <div class="chapter__inner">
    <h2 class="section-title">How the system works</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      <b>Tools are the interface. The system is the operating model.</b>
      One shared layer of signals, logic, and guardrails runs across tools — so decisions stay consistent, work routes correctly, and automation remains reviewable.
    </p>

    <div class="grid3" aria-label="Architecture blocks">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Signals</h3>
        <p class="muted">Comparable inputs captured across workflows so drift, bottlenecks, and impact can be measured consistently.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Throughput, pass-through, and SLAs</li>
          <li>Open-text themes and reasons</li>
          <li>Capacity constraints across recruiter, hiring manager, and interview loops</li>
          <li>Risk indicators and drift signals</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="deepLink" href="/system/signals/">Signals deep dive →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <p class="muted">Rules that turn signals into action — with thresholds, tradeoffs, and escalation paths made explicit.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Expected ranges and alert thresholds</li>
          <li>Root-cause prompts</li>
          <li>Recommended actions and tradeoffs</li>
          <li>Escalation as stakes increase</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="deepLink" href="/system/logic/">Logic deep dive →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Action</h3>
        <p class="muted">Actions happen inside the tools — and every action is visible, logged, and attributable.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Receipts attached to recommendations</li>
          <li>Approvals where needed</li>
          <li>Action logs and change history</li>
          <li>Clear "why this happened" context</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="deepLink" href="/system/operating-model/">Operations deep dive →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

